Chapter: BuiltinShadowZeroArg
  cites Codex chapter General
  cites Codex chapter Numbers

 Probe for the user-arity-beats-builtin dispatch at the arity-0 boundary.
 `abs` is normally a 1-arg Integer builtin. A 0-arg user def with the same
 name must override — pre-fix, `lookup-x86-arity ... <= 0` incorrectly
 treated arity-0 as non-overriding and routed to the 1-arg emit-abs-builtin
 with zero args, emitting a list-at on an empty list. Post-fix (`< 0`),
 only the genuine "not in user-arities" case (-1 sentinel from
 lookup-x86-arity) triggers builtin dispatch.

 Also exercises the negative case: `negate` is not shadowed, so its
 1-arg builtin emit fires normally.

Section: Definitions

  abs : Integer = 99

  opening : Integer = abs + negate 7

